# Row-Level Security (RLS) & Performance Strategy

## Overview
All data is **project-scoped and role-based**. Users access data through project membership with three roles: `owner`, `editor`, `viewer`. Service role (Cron Jobs, Backend Functions) has unrestricted access for automated tasks.

## Collaboration & Roles

### Project Members Table
```typescript
// src/backend/db/tables/project-members.ts
import { pgTable, uuid, text, timestamp, uniqueIndex } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";
import { project } from "./project";
import { users } from "./user";

export const projectMembers = pgTable("project_members", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  projectId: uuid("project_id").references(() => project.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }).notNull(),
  userId: uuid("user_id").references(() => users.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }).notNull(),
  role: text("role", { enum: ["owner", "editor", "viewer"] }).notNull(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow(),
}, (table) => ({
  projectUserUnique: uniqueIndex("project_members_project_user_unique").on(table.projectId, table.userId),
}));
```

### Role Permissions Matrix

| Table | Owner | Editor | Viewer | Service Role |
|-------|-------|--------|--------|--------------|
| **projects** | RW | R | R | RW |
| **project_members** | RW | N | N | RW |
| **keywords** | RW | RW | R | RW |
| **integrations** | RW* | R* | N | RW |
| **analytics_metrics** | R | R | R | RW |
| **traffic_sources** | R | R | R | RW |
| **search_console_metrics** | R | R | R | RW |
| **ai_crawler_logs** | R | R | R | RW |
| **ai_search** | RW | RW | R | RW |
| **icp_profiles** | RW | RW | R | RW |

**Notes:**
- `*` = `integrations` table: Metadata readable, tokens (accessToken, refreshToken) always hidden
- `N` = No access at all

## RLS Policies (SQL)

### Helper Function
```sql
-- Check if user has access to project and get their role
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION get_user_project_role(project_id UUID)
RETURNS TEXT AS $$
  SELECT role FROM project_members 
  WHERE project_id = get_user_project_role.project_id 
    AND user_id = auth.uid()
  LIMIT 1;
$$ LANGUAGE SQL SECURITY DEFINER;
```

### Projects Table
```sql
-- View: User owns project or is a member
ALTER TABLE projects ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Users can view projects they own or are members of"
  ON projects FOR SELECT
  USING (
    owner_id = auth.uid()
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = projects.id AND user_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Only owners can update projects"
  ON projects FOR UPDATE
  USING (owner_id = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY "Only owners can delete projects"
  ON projects FOR DELETE
  USING (owner_id = auth.uid());

CREATE POLICY "Service role bypass"
  ON projects FOR ALL
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');
```

### Project Members Table
```sql
ALTER TABLE project_members ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Project owners can manage members"
  ON project_members FOR ALL
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects WHERE id = project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Service role bypass"
  ON project_members FOR ALL
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');
```

### Keywords Table
```sql
ALTER TABLE keywords ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Owners and editors can write; viewers can read"
  ON keywords FOR SELECT
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = keywords.project_id 
        AND user_id = auth.uid() 
        AND role IN ('owner', 'editor', 'viewer')
    )
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = keywords.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Owners and editors can write keywords"
  ON keywords FOR INSERT
  WITH CHECK (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = keywords.project_id 
        AND user_id = auth.uid() 
        AND role IN ('owner', 'editor')
    )
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = keywords.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Owners and editors can update keywords"
  ON keywords FOR UPDATE
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = keywords.project_id 
        AND user_id = auth.uid() 
        AND role IN ('owner', 'editor')
    )
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = keywords.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Service role bypass"
  ON keywords FOR ALL
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');
```

### Analytics Metrics, Traffic Sources, Search Console, AI Crawler Logs (Read-Only)
```sql
-- Same pattern for: analytics_metrics, traffic_sources, search_console_metrics, ai_crawler_logs

ALTER TABLE analytics_metrics ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Project members can read analytics"
  ON analytics_metrics FOR SELECT
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = analytics_metrics.project_id 
        AND user_id = auth.uid()
    )
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = analytics_metrics.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Service role can write analytics"
  ON analytics_metrics FOR INSERT
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');

CREATE POLICY "Service role can update analytics"
  ON analytics_metrics FOR UPDATE
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');
```

### Integrations Table (Tokens Hidden)
```sql
ALTER TABLE integrations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- SELECT returns metadata only (use VIEW or stored proc to filter tokens)
CREATE POLICY "Project owners and editors can view integration metadata"
  ON integrations FOR SELECT
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM project_members 
      WHERE project_id = integrations.project_id 
        AND user_id = auth.uid() 
        AND role IN ('owner', 'editor')
    )
    OR EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = integrations.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Only owners can manage integrations"
  ON integrations FOR INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = integrations.project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );

CREATE POLICY "Service role bypass"
  ON integrations FOR ALL
  USING (auth.role() = 'service_role');

-- VIEW to hide tokens (client-safe)
CREATE VIEW integrations_safe AS
SELECT 
  id,
  project_id,
  provider,
  metadata,
  connected_at,
  updated_at
FROM integrations;
```

