## Audit Trail (Optional but Recommended)

### Purpose
Track sensitive operations for compliance and debugging.

### Audit Logs Table
```typescript
// src/backend/db/tables/audit-logs.ts
import { pgTable, uuid, text, timestamp, jsonb } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";
import { projects } from "./project";
import { users } from "./user";

export const auditLogs = pgTable("audit_logs", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  projectId: uuid("project_id").references(() => projects.id, { onDelete: "cascade" }).notNull(),
  userId: uuid("user_id").references(() => users.id, { onDelete: "set null" }),
  action: text("action").notNull(), // 'CREATE', 'UPDATE', 'DELETE'
  table: text("table").notNull(), // 'integrations', 'keywords', etc.
  recordId: uuid("record_id"),
  changes: jsonb("changes"), // { before: {...}, after: {...} }
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow(),
});
```

### RLS for Audit Logs
```sql
ALTER TABLE audit_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Project owners can view audit logs"
  ON audit_logs FOR SELECT
  USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM projects 
      WHERE id = project_id AND owner_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );
```

### When to Log (Server Actions)
- ✅ Integration connect/disconnect
- ✅ Keyword creation/deletion
- ✅ Project member add/remove
- ❌ Read-only operations (optional)

